  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Takoyaki are cooked in a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "takoyaki pan ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "takoyaki-pan"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ": a moulded pan with round cavities that lets you turn the balls with skewers to build a crispy shell all over. Adding "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "tenkasu",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "tenkasu"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to the batter gives the inside a light, slightly crunchy texture. Makes 32 balls."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use a skewer to rotate each ball a quarter turn as the outer shell sets. The raw batter folds into the centre. This builds a perfect sphere."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
